    <!-- §1 Overview -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="overview">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§1</div>
        <h2>System Overview</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Supervisor Approval Desk is the second tier of the trade claim workflow. A supervisor
        receives queued claims originating from commercial bank operators, reviews automated
        compliance outputs, evaluates the five-gate issuance eligibility matrix, and issues a
        binding decision: approve, reject, return for clarification, or cancel.
      </p>
      <p>
        The desk does not perform manual compliance judgment — it presents the results of automated
        compliance pipeline services and requires the supervisor to acknowledge and act on those
        results. The supervisor cannot override a <code>blocked</code> compliance status; they can
        only pass back to the originator for correction.
      </p>
      <p>
        Supervisor approval triggers a <strong>Protocol-Enforced State Machine</strong>: the
        approve action does not directly grant settlement authority. Instead it writes
        <code>compliance_cleared</code> (human governance layer confirmed), then immediately
        invokes <code>CorridorVerificationService</code> to run an algorithmic corridor headroom
        check. The final outcome is either <code>ready_to_mint</code> — corridor headroom
        confirmed and claim amount earmarked — or <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code>
        — Governor liquidity injection required before minting can proceed. This two-step protocol
        prevents bearerCORE from attempting minting against a depleted corridor reserve.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>
        <strong>Web console (bearerCORE <code>/sandbox</code>) — role-gated &amp; SmartCHEQ-backed.</strong>
        The desk card renders only when <code>DashboardRolesHelper#show_supervisor_card?</code> is true —
        regulator roles always, role-less public demo visitors and CB-node commercial operators for
        testing (flagged with a <strong>[ SANDBOX SIMULATION ]</strong> pill). A dealer-bank
        <code>commercial_institution_operator</code> <strong>never</strong> sees it (Segregation of Duties).
        All approve / reject / re-evaluate fetches target the <strong>SmartCHEQ</strong> API (the identity
        authority), authorized by the Doorkeeper token bound to the session by the central-bank auth bridge;
        the server re-gates every action with <code>authorize_supervisor_action!</code>. A cleared claim shows
        the <strong>Cleared</strong> label, and an expired portal session (8&nbsp;h TTL) surfaces a
        session-expired modal with a "Sign in again →" link rather than a raw
        <code>operator_unidentified</code> error.
      </div></div>

      <div class="dp-pane-grid">
