    <!-- §2 Design Principles -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="principles">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§2</div>
        <h2>Operational Design Principles</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>System-driven, not judgment-driven</strong></td><td>Compliance checks are automated. Supervisor reviews outputs; does not perform manual AML or limit calculations.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Audit-first</strong></td><td>Every supervisor action — including opening a claim — generates an immutable audit record with actor identity and timestamp.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>No self-service override</strong></td><td>Supervisor cannot approve a claim they originated. No single operator can complete both origination and approval steps.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Notes mandatory on rejection</strong></td><td>Reject and Request Clarification actions require non-empty <code>decision_notes</code>. The system rejects the action without notes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Claim locking</strong></td><td>Opening a claim in review mode soft-locks it against concurrent supervisor edits. Stale-lock detection releases after 10 minutes of inactivity.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Deterministic gate evaluation</strong></td><td>The five-gate eligibility result is computed server-side. The UI displays the result; it cannot alter it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Protocol-enforced settlement path</strong></td><td>A supervisor Approve action never directly authorises minting. The corridor protocol verification step runs automatically and must independently confirm headroom before <code>ready_to_mint</code> is set.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Earmark-based reservation</strong></td><td>When a claim reaches <code>ready_to_mint</code>, the claim amount is atomically earmarked in the corridor ledger so concurrent approvals on the same corridor cannot collectively over-commit available headroom.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §3 Pane Specification -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="panes">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§3</div>
        <h2>Pane-Level Specification</h2>
      </div>

      <h3>Left Pane — Pending Items Queue</h3>
      <p>
        Loaded on modal open by <code>loadSupervisorClaims()</code> which calls
        <code>GET /api/v2/trade_claims</code>. Claims are displayed in reverse-creation order
        (most recent first). The queue auto-refreshes on every supervisor action.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Source</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>#</strong></td><td>row index</td><td>1-based display ordinal</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Claim ID</strong></td><td>claim.reference</td><td>TC-{timestamp} or operator-supplied invoice ref</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Institution</strong></td><td>claim.institution.name</td><td>Resolved commercial bank name</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Amount</strong></td><td>claim.amount + claim.currency_code</td><td>Formatted decimal with ISO 4217 suffix</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Corridor</strong></td><td>claim.corridor.code</td><td>e.g. NGA-GHA</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Status</strong></td><td>claim.status</td><td>Colour-coded badge — see status config table in §6</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Submitted</strong></td><td>claim.created_at</td><td>Relative time (e.g. "3m ago")</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h4>Queue Filtering</h4>
      <p>
        <code>applySupervisorFilters()</code> runs on every keystroke in the search input. Filters
        by claim reference, institution name, and invoice reference. Case-insensitive substring match.
        No server round-trip — filters the in-memory <code>supervisorClaims</code> array.
      </p>

      <h4>Claim Selection</h4>
      <p>
        Clicking a claim row calls <code>selectSupervisorClaim(claimId)</code>.
        ID coerced: <code>String(c.id) === String(claimId)</code> to prevent integer/string
        type mismatch. Selected claim data populates the detail panel. Row highlights with
        left-border indicator.
      </p>

      <h3>Middle Pane — Claim Detail Panel</h3>
      <p>Visible only when a claim is selected. Populated from the in-memory claim object resolved via <code>supervisorClaims.find()</code>.</p>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Fields Displayed</th><th>Editability</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Claim Identity</strong></td><td>Reference, Status badge, Created at, Submitted by</td><td>Read-only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Corridor</strong></td><td>Source country → Target country, Corridor code, Asset code, Bloc</td><td>Read-only (snapshot at origination)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Institution</strong></td><td>Institution name, SWIFT code, Country code</td><td>Read-only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Trade Details</strong></td><td>Amount, Currency, Trade direction, Beneficiary name, Beneficiary country</td><td>Read-only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Description</strong></td><td>Free-text trade description from originator</td><td>Read-only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Five-Gate Matrix</strong></td><td>Supervisor Approval, Compliance, Corridor Limits, Liquidity, Governance — each with passed/pending indicator and gate note</td><td>System-computed; read-only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Verification Note</strong></td><td>Corridor protocol check result from CorridorVerificationService (headroom confirmed or shortfall details)</td><td>Read-only; populated after approve action</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Decision Notes</strong></td><td>Text area for supervisor to record reasoning</td><td>Editable — required for Reject and Request Clarification</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Prior Decisions</strong></td><td>Approved/rejected/clarification history with timestamps if previously actioned</td><td>Read-only</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Right Pane — Action Panel</h3>
      <p>Action buttons visible only when a claim is selected. Button availability governed by current claim status. Terminal states are: <code>ready_to_mint</code>, <code>rejected</code>, <code>cancelled</code>.</p>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Enabled When</th><th>Disabled / Blocked When</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Approve</strong></td><td>status == pending_review AND compliance != blocked</td><td>Any terminal state OR compliance == blocked</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Reject</strong></td><td>status NOT in [ready_to_mint, rejected, cancelled]</td><td>status in [ready_to_mint, rejected, cancelled] — these are terminal states</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Request Clarification</strong></td><td>status NOT in [ready_to_mint, rejected, cancelled]</td><td>Terminal states</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Cancel</strong></td><td>Any status including ready_to_mint</td><td>status == cancelled only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Re-Evaluate</strong></td><td>status == insufficient_corridor_liquidity (Governor escape hatch)</td><td>Other statuses (no-op if called outside liquidity-insufficient state)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn">
        <span class="dp-ci">⚠</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Cancel on ready_to_mint:</strong> Cancelling a claim that has reached
          <code>ready_to_mint</code> automatically releases the earmarked corridor headroom back
          to the corridor reserve. This is the correct cancellation path — the earmark is never
          left orphaned.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §4 Compliance Pipeline -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="compliance">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§4</div>
        <h2>Automated Compliance Pipeline</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        When a claim enters <code>pending_review</code>, the compliance pipeline runs automatically.
        The supervisor desk displays the pipeline result; the supervisor does not trigger or
        re-run individual checks.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>DocumentValidationService → document_status</h4><p>Validates invoice reference format and completeness. Checks for required trade documentation fields. Returns: valid | incomplete | missing.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>AMLCheckService → aml_status</h4><p>Screens beneficiary name and country against AU-maintained watchlists. Jurisdiction risk scoring for destination country. Returns: clear | flagged | blocked.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>LimitCheckService → limit_status</h4><p>Validates amount against active corridor limits: per-transaction cap, daily cap utilisation, velocity (rolling 1-hour) window. Returns: within_limits | approaching_limit | exceeded.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>BeneficiaryVerificationService → beneficiary_status</h4><p>Cross-references beneficiary name against registered beneficiary registry. Country consistency check. Returns: verified | unverified | mismatch.</p></div>
        <div class="dp-step"><h4>ComplianceStatusAggregator → compliance_status</h4><p>Aggregates all four service results. Returns: pre_cleared | manual_review | blocked. A single blocked sub-result produces a blocked aggregate.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Aggregate Status</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Supervisor Can Approve</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="s-active">pre_cleared</span></td><td>All sub-checks passed. No flags.</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="s-pending">manual_review</span></td><td>One or more sub-checks flagged. No block.</td><td>Yes — supervisor assumes responsibility</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="s-expired">blocked</span></td><td>At least one sub-check returned blocked.</td><td>No — must return to originator</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §5 Five Gates -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="gates">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§5</div>
        <h2>Five-Gate Issuance Eligibility</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The supervisor's approve action triggers a two-step protocol (see §6). The five-gate
        eligibility result is returned in the response body under the <code>eligibility</code>
        key. All five gates must return <code>passed: true</code> for
        <code>issuance_eligible</code> to be true — which only occurs when status is
        <code>ready_to_mint</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Evaluated By</th><th>Pass Condition</th><th>Fail Consequence</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>supervisor_approval</strong></td>
            <td>Supervisor Desk action</td>
            <td>Supervisor has called <code>/approve</code> (status is compliance_cleared, ready_to_mint, or insufficient_corridor_liquidity)</td>
            <td>Issuance blocked until supervisor acts</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>compliance</strong></td>
            <td>ComplianceStatusAggregator</td>
            <td>Aggregate status is pre_cleared or manual_review</td>
            <td>Issuance blocked; claim returned to originator</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>corridor_limits</strong></td>
            <td>CorridorVerificationService</td>
            <td>Corridor is not halted AND status is ready_to_mint</td>
            <td>Issuance blocked; Governor must resume halted corridor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>liquidity</strong></td>
            <td>CorridorVerificationService — net headroom check</td>
            <td>free_headroom (domestic_available − linked_outstanding − existing_earmarks) ≥ claim amount</td>
            <td>Status set to insufficient_corridor_liquidity; Governor liquidity injection required</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>governance</strong></td>
            <td>Corridor protocol verification</td>
            <td>No open halt proposals or freeze orders; status is ready_to_mint</td>
            <td>Issuance blocked until governance action resolved</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Re-Evaluate — Governor Escape Hatch</h3>
      <p>
        <code>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/re_evaluate</code> is specifically designed for
        claims in <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code>. When the Governor injects
        liquidity into a corridor, the corridor's net headroom increases. Re-evaluate re-runs
        <code>CorridorVerificationService</code> against the current position:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>If headroom now covers the claim amount → status advances to <code>ready_to_mint</code> and the amount is earmarked. No resubmission required.</li>
        <li>If headroom is still insufficient → status remains <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code> with an updated verification note showing current shortfall.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Re-evaluate has no effect on claims in other states — it only does meaningful work
        when status is <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn">
        <span class="dp-ci">⚠</span>
        <div>
          A claim approved at time T may reach <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code>
          if other claims were simultaneously approved against the same corridor and consumed
          the remaining headroom. Supervisors should re-evaluate before approving claims that
          have been queued for extended periods — corridor positions change in real time.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §6 Protocol-Enforced State Machine -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="state-machine">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§6</div>
        <h2>Protocol-Enforced State Machine</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The approval pipeline is a two-step state machine. Jumping straight to a settled/minted
        state would allow bearerCORE to attempt minting against a depleted corridor reserve — the
        two-step protocol prevents this.
      </p>

      <div class="dp-flow">
        <div class="dp-step">
          <h4>Step 0 — pending_review</h4>
          <p>Claim submitted by commercial bank operator. Compliance pipeline runs automatically. Supervisor desk loads the claim in the queue. No corridor headroom has been reserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-step">
          <h4>Step 1 — compliance_cleared  <span style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:#6b7280;">(human governance layer)</span></h4>
          <p>Supervisor calls <code>POST /approve</code>. Server writes <code>compliance_cleared</code> and <code>compliance_cleared_at</code> timestamp. Decision notes recorded if provided. This is the human sign-off — it confirms the supervisor has reviewed the claim and authorised it to proceed to algorithmic verification.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-step">
          <h4>Step 2 — CorridorVerificationService  <span style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:#6b7280;">(algorithmic layer, runs automatically)</span></h4>
          <p>
            Invoked immediately after Step 1. Reads the live corridor position from
            <code>STUB_CORRIDORS</code>, checks the halted-corridor set, reads the
            allocation ledger (reflecting Governor injections and HANDSHAKE_WINDOW-elapsed
            pending allocations), then computes:<br><br>
            <code>net_headroom = domestic_available − linked_outstanding</code><br>
            <code>free_headroom = net_headroom − existing_earmarks[corridor_id]</code>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-step" style="border-left-color:#10b981;">
          <h4>→ ready_to_mint  <span style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:#059669;">(terminal — minting authorised)</span></h4>
          <p>
            If <code>free_headroom ≥ claim_amount</code>: status set to <code>ready_to_mint</code>.
            The claim amount is atomically added to <code>CorridorVerificationService.earmarks[corridor_id]</code>
            so no subsequent claim can double-count this headroom. The response includes
            <code>earmarked_amount</code>, <code>corridor_headroom_at_verification</code>, and
            <code>asset_code</code>. bearerCORE issuance is now authorised against this claim.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-step" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b;">
          <h4>→ insufficient_corridor_liquidity  <span style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:#92400e;">(awaiting Governor injection)</span></h4>
          <p>
            If <code>free_headroom &lt; claim_amount</code>, or if the corridor is halted:
            status set to <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code>. The response includes
            <code>shortfall</code> (the gap to fill), <code>corridor_headroom_at_verification</code>,
            and <code>verification_note</code> with human-readable explanation.
            The Governor's Desk must inject liquidity into the corridor before the claim
            can advance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="dp-step" style="border-left-color:#3b82f6;">
          <h4>Re-Evaluate (after Governor injection)</h4>
          <p>
            Supervisor calls <code>POST /re_evaluate</code>. <code>CorridorVerificationService</code>
            re-runs Step 2 against the updated corridor position. If liquidity has been injected
            and headroom now covers the claim, status advances to <code>ready_to_mint</code> and
            the earmark is written. If still insufficient, status remains unchanged with an
            updated shortfall note.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>State Transition Summary</h3>
      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Colour</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Terminal?</th><th>Next Action</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>pending_review</code></td><td>Grey</td><td>In queue, awaiting supervisor</td><td>No</td><td>Supervisor approves / rejects / clarifies / cancels</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>compliance_cleared</code></td><td>Blue</td><td>Human layer signed off; corridor check in progress</td><td>No</td><td>Automatic (CorridorVerificationService runs immediately)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>ready_to_mint</code></td><td>Green</td><td>Corridor confirmed; amount earmarked; minting authorised</td><td>Yes</td><td>bearerCORE minting; or Cancel (releases earmark)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code></td><td>Amber</td><td>Headroom depleted; awaiting Governor injection</td><td>No</td><td>Governor injects liquidity → Re-Evaluate; or Cancel</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>clarification_requested</code></td><td>Orange</td><td>Returned to originator for correction</td><td>No</td><td>Originator corrects and resubmits → pending_review</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>rejected</code></td><td>Red</td><td>Declined by supervisor</td><td>Yes</td><td>Originator creates new claim</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cancelled</code></td><td>Dark grey</td><td>Cancelled (earmark released if applicable)</td><td>Yes</td><td>None</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <h3>Earmark Ledger</h3>
      <p>
        <code>CorridorVerificationService</code> maintains a class-level ledger:
        <code>@earmarks = Hash.new(0)</code> — a map of corridor ID to total earmarked
        amount. When a claim reaches <code>ready_to_mint</code>, its amount is added to
        the ledger atomically. When a <code>ready_to_mint</code> claim is cancelled, the
        amount is subtracted via <code>CorridorVerificationService.release_earmark(corridor_id, amount)</code>.
        This ensures all concurrent approve actions on the same corridor see an accurate
        free headroom figure and cannot collectively over-commit the available reserve.
      </p>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info">
        <span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span>
        <div>
          The earmark ledger is in-process memory (no database). It persists for the lifetime
          of the Rails server process and resets on server restart. In production this would
          be backed by a persistent atomic store (Redis, distributed lock, or database row).
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §7 Action Buttons -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="buttons">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§7</div>
        <h2>Action Button Specification</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Approve</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Decision Action — triggers two-step protocol</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Enabled</div><div>status == pending_review AND compliance_status != blocked</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Notes</div><div>Optional — supervisor may add approval notes</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/approve {notes: "..."}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Step 1</div><div>Server writes status: compliance_cleared + compliance_cleared_at. Human governance layer confirmed.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Step 2</div><div>CorridorVerificationService runs immediately and sets final status to ready_to_mint or insufficient_corridor_liquidity.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Response — ready_to_mint</div><div>status: "ready_to_mint", eligibility: {issuance_eligible: true, all 5 gates passed: true}, message: "READY TO MINT. bearerCORE issuance authorised."</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Response — liquidity insufficient</div><div>status: "insufficient_corridor_liquidity", eligibility: {issuance_eligible: false, liquidity gate: failed}, message: "⚠ Corridor protocol check failed: [shortfall details]. Governor liquidity injection required."</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">UI — ready_to_mint</div><div>Green result modal. Status badge → Ready to Mint. Five-gate panel shows all gates passed with notes (headroom confirmed, amount earmarked). Action buttons disable. Queue refreshes.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">UI — liquidity insufficient</div><div>Amber result modal with verification_note (shortfall details) and Governor injection instructions. Re-Evaluate button activates. Claim remains visible in queue.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Audit</div><div>TradeClaimComplianceCleared event at Step 1. CorridorProtocolVerified or CorridorLiquidityInsufficient event at Step 2. Full gate snapshot recorded.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Downstream</div><div>bearerCORE minting is authorised only when status is ready_to_mint. Compliance-cleared alone is not sufficient — the corridor protocol must also pass.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Reject</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Decision Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Notes</div><div>Mandatory — submit blocked until notes field is non-empty</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Enabled</div><div>status NOT in [ready_to_mint, rejected, cancelled]</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/reject {notes: "..."}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Response</div><div>status: rejected, data: claim record with rejected_at and decision_notes</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>Claim removed from active queue. Terminal state — cannot be reversed.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Notification</div><div>Originating operator notified of rejection with supervisor notes.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Audit</div><div>TradeClaimRejected event written. Notes stored immutably on claim record.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Request Clarification</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Routing Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Notes</div><div>Mandatory — supervisor must specify what clarification is needed</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/request_clarification {notes: "..."}</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect</div><div>Status → clarification_requested. Claim moves to originator's pending action queue.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Recovery</div><div>Originator corrects and resubmits → status reverts to pending_review.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Timeout</div><div>Claims in clarification_requested for &gt;7 days trigger supervisor manager alert.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Re-Evaluate</span><span class="dp-btn-pane m">Governor Escape Hatch</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Purpose</div><div>Advance a claim from insufficient_corridor_liquidity to ready_to_mint after Governor has injected corridor liquidity.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Enabled</div><div>status == insufficient_corridor_liquidity</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/re_evaluate</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect — headroom restored</div><div>CorridorVerificationService re-runs. If free_headroom ≥ claim_amount: status → ready_to_mint, earmark written. No resubmission required.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect — still insufficient</div><div>Status remains insufficient_corridor_liquidity. verification_note updated with current shortfall figure. Governor must inject more.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">UI Update</div><div>Five-gate panel refreshes with updated gate results and verification note.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-btn">
        <div class="dp-btn-head"><span class="dp-btn-name">Cancel Claim</span><span class="dp-btn-pane r">Destructive Action</span></div>
        <div class="dp-btn-body">
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Confirmation</div><div>Confirmation prompt shown before proceeding</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">API</div><div>POST /api/v2/trade_claims/:id/cancel</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Enabled</div><div>Any status (no terminal-state block on cancel)</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect — ready_to_mint claim</div><div>Earmark released via CorridorVerificationService.release_earmark(corridor_id, earmarked_amount). Corridor headroom restored for other claims. Status → cancelled.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Effect — other statuses</div><div>Status → cancelled. cancelled_at timestamp written. No earmark to release.</div></div>
          <div class="dp-btn-row"><div class="dp-btn-lbl">Reversibility</div><div>Terminal — cannot be undone. Originator must create a new claim.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §8 Concurrency -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="concurrency">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§8</div>
        <h2>Concurrency &amp; Multi-User Handling</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Resolution</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Two supervisors open same claim</strong></td>
            <td>Soft lock written on first open. Second supervisor sees "Under Review by [operator]" indicator.</td>
            <td>Second supervisor can view but action buttons are disabled. Lock releases after 10 minutes of first supervisor inactivity.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Concurrent approvals on same corridor</strong></td>
            <td>Earmark ledger (<code>CorridorVerificationService.@earmarks</code>) tracks total earmarked per corridor. Each approval deducts from free headroom before writing the earmark.</td>
            <td>First approval earmarks the headroom. Second approval may find insufficient free headroom and reach <code>insufficient_corridor_liquidity</code> even if the first claim passed. Correct by design — the corridor reserve is not over-committed.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Originator cancels while supervisor reviews</strong></td>
            <td>Cancel writes terminal status immediately. Supervisor action on a cancelled claim returns HTTP 422 with terminal state error.</td>
            <td>Supervisor desk shows "Claim is in terminal state: cancelled." Queue refreshes.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Stale queue data</strong></td>
            <td>Queue loaded at modal open. New claims submitted after load are not visible until refresh.</td>
            <td>Manual refresh button re-calls <code>GET /api/v2/trade_claims</code>. Auto-refresh every 30s in production implementation.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Double-click approve</strong></td>
            <td>Button disabled immediately on first click while request is in flight.</td>
            <td>Server validates terminal state before acting — a second approve call on a ready_to_mint or rejected claim returns HTTP 422 unprocessable_entity.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Network failure mid-action</strong></td>
            <td>Client catches fetch error and displays inline error. No state change on server.</td>
            <td>Supervisor retries. If the first request had already succeeded server-side, the second call hits the terminal-state guard and returns the current record without double-writing.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>

      <div class="dp-callout dp-danger">
        <span class="dp-ci">⛔</span>
        <div>
          <strong>No self-approval:</strong> The system must enforce that the operator who submitted a
          trade claim cannot be the supervisor who approves it. In the current implementation this is
          an operational control enforced by RBAC role assignment — the submitting operator does not
          have Supervisor role access to the desk. Production implementations should add explicit
          server-side originator ≠ approver validation.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- §9 Events -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="events">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§9</div>
        <h2>System Events</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="dp-table-wrap"><table class="dp-table">
